  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 218 AM EST Thu Nov 19 2026\n\nAs we start the weekend, the aforementioned surface low is expected \nto move up the Eastern Seaboard, removing its influence from the \nlocal area. The southern stream is forecast to shift north across \nthe southern third of the CONUS resulting, locally, in mostly zonal \nflow aloft at the base of a broad full CONUS trough. Global \nensembles are in rather good agreement in this evolution through \nearly next week. They begin to diverge a bit around mid-week when \nthe pattern amplifies a bit and a shortwave moves across the \ncountry bringing our next best chance of rain. We should be able \nto squeeze out 2 or 3 relatively dry days before then though. \nSeasonable temperatures are expected late this weekend through \nearly next week.",
